          %h2#idea Idea
          %p
            There is a sense in which a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sheaf"} sheaf
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi F
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F
            is like a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/categorification"} categorification
            of a
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/function"} function
            = succeed "-map" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/stalk"} stalk
            = succeed "s" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/point+of+a+topos"} topos point
            = succeed "s" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/set"} set
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msup
                    %mi x
                    %mo *
                  %mo ⊣
                  %msub
                    %mi x
                    %mo *
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ↦
                  %mi F
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi x
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo :
                  %mo =
                  %msup
                    %mi x
                    %mo *
                  %mi F
                  %mo ∈
                  %mi Set
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (x^* \dashv x_*) \mapsto F(x) := x^* F \in Set
            under
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/decategorification"} decategorification
            as a
            = succeed "-valued" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cardinality"} cardinality
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/function"} function
          %p
            Under this interpretation, many constructions in
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category+theory"} category theory
            have analogs in
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/linear+algebra"} linear algebra
            = succeed "s" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/product"} product
            = succeed "s)" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/limit"} limit
            = succeed "s" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/coproduct"} coproduct
            = succeed "s)." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/colimit"} colimit
            = succeed "-preserving" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/colimit"} colimit
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/functor"} functor
            between
            = succeed "es" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sheaf+topos"} sheaf topos
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/linear+map"} linear map
            or to a
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/distribution"} distribution
            = succeed "s." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lawvere+distribution"} Lawvere distribution
          %p
            This
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/categorification"} categorification
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/linear+algebra"} linear algebra
            becomes even better behaved if we pass all the way to
            = succeed "es." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-sheaf+%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-topos"} (∞,1)-sheaf (∞,1)-topos
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%E2%88%9E-groupoid+cardinality"} ∞-groupoid cardinality
            their
            = succeed "s" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/stalk"} stalk
            = succeed "s," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/integer"} integer
            = succeed "s," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/rational+number"} rational number
            = succeed "s." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/real+number"} real number
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Goodwillie+calculus"} Goodwillie calculus
          %p
            A
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/span"} span
            of
            = succeed "s" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/base+change+geometric+morphism"} base change geometric morphism
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/linear+map"} linear map
            given by a
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/matrix"} matrix
            = succeed "s" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/integral+transform"} integral transform
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Fourier-Mukai+transform"} Fourier-Mukai transform
            which categorifies the
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Fourier+transform"} Fourier transform
          %p
            These analogies have been noticed and exploited at various places in the literature. See for instance the entries
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/groupoidification"} groupoidification
            or
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/geometric+%E2%88%9E-function+theory"} geometric ∞-function theory
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-topos+theory"} (∞,1)-topos theoretic
            description with examples from ordinary
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topos+theory"} topos theory
            to motivate the constructions.
          %h2#linear_bases Linear bases
          %p
            Every
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-topos"} (∞,1)-topos
            is a
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/locally+presentable+%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-category"} locally presentable (∞,1)-category
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-categories"} (∞,1)-categories
            as being analogous to
            = succeed "s" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/vector+space"} vector space
            = succeed "s." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/linear+functional"} linear functional
          .un_prop
            %h6#proposition Proposition
            %p
              Every
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/locally+presentable+%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-category"} locally presentable (∞,1)-category
              is a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/reflective+sub-%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-category"} reflective sub-(∞,1)-category
              of an
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-category+of+%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-presheaves"} (∞,1)-category of (∞,1)-presheaves
          %p
            See
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/locally+presentable+%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-category"} locally presentable (∞,1)-category
            for details.
          .un_remark
            %h6#remark Remark
            %p
              For
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
              a small
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-category"} (∞,1)-category
              the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-category+of+%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-presheaves"} (∞,1)-category of (∞,1)-presheaves
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mover
                      %mi C
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ^
                    %mo :
                    %mo =
                    %mi Func
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msup
                      %mi C
                      %mi op
                    %mo ,
                    %mn ∞
                    %mi Grpd
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\hat C := Func(C^{op}, \infty Grpd)
            %p
              is the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/free+cocompletion"} free (∞,1)-cocompletion
              of
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi C
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
              = succeed "s." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-colimit"} (∞,1)-colimit
              %em spanned
              by the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/basis"} basis
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi C
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
            %p
              Accordingly an arbitrary locally presentable
              = succeed "-category" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mn ∞
                      %mo ,
                      %mn 1
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\infty,1)
          .un_prop
            %h6#proposition_2 Proposition
            %p
              For
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mover
                      %mi C
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ^
                    %mo ,
                    %mover
                      %mi D
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ^
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \hat C, \hat D
              two
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-categories+of+%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-presheaves"} (∞,1)-categories of (∞,1)-presheaves
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mover
                      %mi C
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ^
                    %mo →
                    %mover
                      %mi D
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ^
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \hat C \to \hat D
              in
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Pr%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29Cat"} Pr(∞,1)Cat
              is equivalently a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-profunctor"} (∞,1)-profunctor
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi C
                      %mi ⇸
                      %mi D
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C  &amp;#8696; D
          %p
            See
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/profunctor"} profunctor
            for details.
          %h2#homspaces Hom-spaces
          .un_prop
            %h6#proposition_3 Proposition
            %p
              For
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi C
                    %mo ,
                    %mi D
                    %mo ∈
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C, D \in
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Pr%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29Cat"} Pr(∞,1)Cat
              we have that
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi Func
                      %mi L
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi C
                    %mo ,
                    %mi D
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Func^L(C,D)
              is itself locally presentable.
          %p
            See
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Pr%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29Cat"} Pr(∞,1)Cat
            for details.
          .un_remark
            %h6#remark_2 Remark
            %p
              This means that to the extent that we may think of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi C
                    %mo ,
                    %mi D
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C, D
              as analogous to vector spaces, also the space of linear maps between them is analogous to a vector space.
          %h2#tensor_products Tensor products
          .un_prop
            %h6#fact Fact
            %p
              For
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
              and
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi D
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} D
              two
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/locally+presentable+%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-categories"} locally presentable (∞,1)-categories
              there is locally presentable
              = succeed "-category" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mn ∞
                      %mo ,
                      %mn 1
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\infty,1)
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi C
                    %mo ⊗
                    %mi D
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C \otimes D
              and an
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-functor"} (∞,1)-functor
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi C
                    %mo ×
                    %mi D
                    %mo →
                    %mi C
                    %mo ⊗
                    %mi D
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    C \times D \to C \otimes D
            %p
              which is
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/universal+property"} universal
              with respect to the property that it preserves
              = succeed "s" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-colimit"} (∞,1)-colimit
          .un_remark
            %h6#remark_3 Remark
            %p
              This means that in as far as
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi C
                    %mo ,
                    %mi D
                    %mo ∈
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C, D \in
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Pr%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29Cat"} Pr(∞,1)Cat
              are analogous to vector spaces,
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi C
                    %mo ⊗
                    %mi D
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C \otimes D
              is analogous to their
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/tensor+product"} tensor product
          %h2#FunctionSpaces Function spaces
          %p
            We consider from now on some fixed ambient
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-topos"} (∞,1)-topos
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
